  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-1",
      "transcript": "How can light reveal an obstacle without being absorbed or reflected by it?",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 5.3,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.b5a7d5e28a01e089655359e9920607de1e175de741aef264c289f18affd10001",
        "sha256": "b5a7d5e28a01e089655359e9920607de1e175de741aef264c289f18affd10001"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-2",
      "transcript": "Send one photon into an interferometer: two possible paths, joined again.",
      "start": 5.666666666666667,
      "duration": 5.525,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.5c94b4c807463a6b21e105b206889c354a945a8adead2d347b2c34888faf55a9",
        "sha256": "5c94b4c807463a6b21e105b206889c354a945a8adead2d347b2c34888faf55a9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-3",
      "transcript": "With both paths open and the device correctly aligned, interference keeps one detector dark.",
      "start": 11.4,
      "duration": 6.425,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.2f25a7a958cff95e90d4cccc6faeeb319d079db0f9cf987760e7dc525e71ebe2",
        "sha256": "2f25a7a958cff95e90d4cccc6faeeb319d079db0f9cf987760e7dc525e71ebe2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-4",
      "transcript": "The waves associated with the two paths cancel at that output.",
      "start": 18.033333333333335,
      "duration": 4.375,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.5267a407e3e7a09d46838fc22f6566bd9617b217554073d675aa4879775aba7e",
        "sha256": "5267a407e3e7a09d46838fc22f6566bd9617b217554073d675aa4879775aba7e"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-5",
      "transcript": "Now put a light-absorbing object in one path. If it absorbs the photon, neither output detector clicks.",
      "start": 22.633333333333333,
      "duration": 7.4,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.ba0a7d0e0b8f83acc20a9bbbb314fe90fe821cf811a494cb438336ac3125b4d7",
        "sha256": "ba0a7d0e0b8f83acc20a9bbbb314fe90fe821cf811a494cb438336ac3125b4d7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-6",
      "transcript": "But sometimes the formerly dark detector clicks instead.",
      "start": 30.233333333333334,
      "duration": 4,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.887f1e77873dbb0569e499893fe5f694ecda3c57d47668f43c7feabb6384b9cc",
        "sha256": "887f1e77873dbb0569e499893fe5f694ecda3c57d47668f43c7feabb6384b9cc"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-7",
      "transcript": "That single photon reached the detector, so the object did not absorb it. The blocked path removed the cancellation.",
      "start": 34.6,
      "duration": 7.9,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.38a097ee674802afab320f78d11fee6afa5e505e9885011af00ef83b1be9a938",
        "sha256": "38a097ee674802afab320f78d11fee6afa5e505e9885011af00ef83b1be9a938"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-8",
      "transcript": "The click reveals the obstacle. Other trials absorb the photon or give no clear answer. This is not a guaranteed harmless test.",
      "start": 42.7,
      "duration": 9.55,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.fdf71b892d0dc6222ad42b47d2212a94f4fb2edd015b203da278128ce7398bd6",
        "sha256": "fdf71b892d0dc6222ad42b47d2212a94f4fb2edd015b203da278128ce7398bd6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ifm-cue-9",
      "transcript": "Researchers have demonstrated this effect, called interaction-free measurement. The clue comes from changing which paths are available.",
      "start": 52.46666666666667,
      "duration": 8.375,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.404625f682738f2813b83b5b8c954090c40e5437672553a41b54bbee45d249b5",
        "sha256": "404625f682738f2813b83b5b8c954090c40e5437672553a41b54bbee45d249b5"
      }
    }
  ],
